To focus on an element found by `getElementsByTagName` in JavaScript, you can use the `focus()` method on the element. Here is an example:
```
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName("input"); // or "button", etc.
var targetElement = elements[0]; // select the first element
targetElement.focus(); // focus on the element
```
This will focus on the first element found by `getElementsByTagName`. If you want to focus on a specific element, you can use a loop to iterate through the elements and find the one you want:
```
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName("input");
for (var i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
    var element = elements[i];
    if (element.id === "myElement") { // or use another condition to select the element
        element.focus();
        break;
    }
}
```
Note that the `focus()` method only works on elements that can be focused, such as input fields, buttons, and links. If you try to focus on an element that cannot be focused, the method will not have any effect.

